# Visible-content descriptions for the 78 pictures. Written from viewing each picture; no prior reports used.
D = {
"CH01-SET-001-ST01_V001.jpg": "Elevated view at dawn or dusk of a walled earthen compound. Round thatched huts with conical roofs fill the foreground, with mud walls and blue patterned bands. A large central hall with a tall thatched roof and wooden verandah posts sits at the back. Ground mist, orange horizon, stake field and forest beyond. No people.",
"CH01-SET-001-ST02_V001.jpg": "Elevated view in overcast daylight of a compound with an open beaten-earth court. Two carved standing wooden figures stand in the centre. A mud building with two round towers and a thatched roof stands at upper centre, with stairs to its entrance. Round thatched huts sit within curved walls; a blue geometric panel is on a gate. No people.",
"CH01-SET-001-ST03_V001.jpg": "Sunset view with a low orange sun on the horizon and warm raking light across a courtyard. A rectangular mud building with triangle and diamond patterns on its facade has a doorway and steps. Round thatched huts with blue woven hangings line the court; rubble lies at the right edge. No people.",
"CH01-SET-001-ST04_V001.jpg": "Night scene under a starry sky with blue-toned light and warm lamp glow in doorways. A tall multi-storey mud building with pointed finials and blue patterned panels stands at upper right. Thatched huts with lit doorways, blue textile hangings, and a wooden stake fence in the foreground. No people.",
"CH01-SET-001-ST05_V001.jpg": "Heavy rain over a wet, reflective ground with puddles and light shafts through cloud. A long low building with thatched roofs and a central gabled entrance hung with dark cloth sits at centre-right. A large thatched hut in the foreground has blue cloth draped over its walls. No people.",
"CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_BACK_V001_REFERENCE_VS_CANDIDATE.jpg": "Two-panel comparison sheet on a dark UI background. The left panel is a master identity reference with a front portrait, detail crops and identity-lock text. The right panel is a grey studio render of a figure seen from behind: braids in a high knot, bare shoulders, indigo bandeau top, indigo wrap skirt with a knot at the back, diagonal leather strap, bronze armlet, leather sandals. Banner text reads back reference versus new candidate, marked unapproved, pending CD/TD review.",
"CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_FRONT_V001_REFERENCE_VS_CANDIDATE.jpg": "Two-panel comparison sheet on a dark UI background. The left panel is the same master identity reference. The right panel is a front reference view on grey with a height scale from 1 to 7.5 heads and callouts: high knot micro-braids, temple beads, indigo bandeau, studded leather baldric, stitched scabbard at the left hip, indigo wrapper skirt, spiral bronze pendant, coiled bronze armlet on the left arm, plain leather sandals. Banner marks the candidate as unapproved, pending review.",
"CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_LEFT_SIDE_V001_REFERENCE_VS_CANDIDATE.jpg": "Two-panel comparison sheet on a dark UI background. The left panel is the same master identity reference. The right panel is a reference plate titled left profile on grey: a full-length side-on figure with a high knot, indigo bandeau, indigo wrap skirt and a bronze armlet on the upper arm, standing barefoot. Banner marks the candidate as unapproved, pending review.",
"CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_THREE_QUARTER_V001_REFERENCE_VS_CANDIDATE.jpg": "Two-panel comparison sheet on a dark UI background. The left panel is the same master identity reference. The right panel is a production model sheet on grey, labelled three-quarter front: a full figure with a high knot, indigo bandeau, indigo wrap skirt, a diagonal leather baldric across the torso, a scabbard hilt at the left hip, a bronze armlet and leather sandals. Banner marks the candidate as unapproved, pending review.",
"COSTUME_BREAKDOWN_SHEET_V001_REFERENCE_VS_CANDIDATE.jpg": "Two-panel comparison sheet. The left panel is the master identity reference. The right panel is a costume breakdown titled CHAR_ADANNA_COSTUME_BREAKDOWN_V001, marked unapproved, pending CD. It shows a front figure with callouts (scar on left cheek, spiral pendant, indigo wrap top, leather strap and stud, hip-scabbard position on the left hip), a back-view panel stamped UNRESOLVED, NOT APPROVED, a right-side panel marked plain by design, and crops of the temple beads and coiled armlet. A bottom line lists unresolved areas. Footer: candidate only, not for promotion.",
"ENV_CH03-INT-004_THE_FORGOTTEN_KITCHEN_V001.jpg": "Dim interior with weathered, cracked plaster walls and no people. A stone cooking stove with two arched fire openings holds a large dark metal pot, with a smaller pot beside it. Dried herb bundles hang from the left wall, and a clay jar sits in a wall niche. In the centre are a stone grinding quern and a woven basket. An open wooden door and a corridor lie at right beside a wooden table with bowls.",
"ENV_CH03-INT-005_A_SLEEPING_ROOM_V001.jpg": "Interior with warm brown plastered walls and no people. A barred wooden shuttered window at left throws light onto a raised wooden platform holding a woven mat and a folded striped cream blanket. At right, a wooden stool holds a dark glazed jug with a brass-rimmed neck and a clay bowl. A small arched niche is set in the wall above.",
"ENV_CH03-SUB-005_A_RESIDENTIAL_COURTYARD_V001.jpg": "Warm daylight courtyard with ochre and red brick walls and no people. A square brick planter holds a tree with a pale trunk and dense leaves. Indigo cloths hang on a line at left. At right, a stone trough has a running tap and a pool of water, beside weathered louvred wooden shutters and a large clay jar. A dark doorway with a stone surround sits at the back.",
"ENV_CH03-SUB-006_THE_BACK_PLOTS_V001.jpg": "Overgrown back yard under an overcast sky, with a row of terrace houses and chimneys behind and no people. A collapsed timber trellis, derelict sheds with corrugated roofs and ivy on the walls are at left. Okra-type plants with pods grow in the foreground, beside a dark compost heap and a rusted metal drum on its side. Faded laundry hangs on a line at right.",
"ENV_CH03-TRV-003_THE_NARROW_PASSAGES_V001.jpg": "Narrow alley with a worn flagstone floor and warm low light from the far end, and no people. Tattered reddish-brown cloth canopies are strung across the alley overhead. Brick and mud walls line both sides, with an arched doorway and a small barred window on the right. The plaster is patched and damaged.",
"ENV_CH04-EXP-003_THE_SMALL_ISLANDS_V001.jpg": "Painted river landscape under a pale overcast sky, with hazy hills on the horizon and no people. Several low islands with palms and grasses sit in a wide river. A large island at upper right carries a dense rounded tree canopy. Three wooden canoes are drawn up on a sandbank at lower right, and broad-leaved vegetation fills the foreground left.",
"ENV_CH04-EXP-006_THE_CAVE_BEHIND_THE_LOW_FALLS_V001.jpg": "Waterfall falling in several sheets over a stone ledge into a pool, with spray in the air and no people. A rock overhang above and behind the falls has a dark recessed cave wall with dripping water lines. Ferns grow on the rock lips and moss covers the ledges. A rainbow arc is visible at upper left.",
"ENV_CH04-INT-001_A_FISHING_SHELTER_V001.jpg": "Open-sided thatched shelter on timber posts, with the river beyond and no people. Fishing nets hang from the roof beams with small weights. Wicker traps and baskets sit at left with a long pole. A plank table holds a knife on a board, and a smoking rack stands over the water at right.",
"ENV_CH04-INT-002_A_RIVERBANK_HOUSE_V001.jpg": "Raised house on timber stilts standing in brown water, with a thatched gable roof and plastered walls, and no people. A rack of drying fish hangs at the front, with clay pots, baskets and a bundle beside it. Inside, a low platform holds a folded mat. A dugout canoe with a woven cover lies at left, and a ladder climbs to the platform.",
"ENV_CH04-INT-003_THE_CANOE_SHED_V001.jpg": "Long open timber shed with a thatched roof and no people. Wooden paddles hang on a plank wall with coiled rope and dark pots on a shelf. Two or three dugout canoes rest on log cradles on the floor. A coil of rope lies in the foreground, and two wooden tubs at lower right hold black tar-like liquid with a stick in it. River and wooded hills show through the open side.",
"ENV_CH04-SET-002_THE_TWO_HOUSE_LANDING_V001.jpg": "Two thatched stilt houses stand either side of a muddy path leading into palm forest, in misty morning light and with no people. The left house has plank walls and a timber ladder. The right house has woven-panel walls, a clay pot by the door, and a ladder. A line strung between posts holds drying leaves or strips. Two dugout boats with bench seats are moored in the water in the foreground.",
"ENV_CH05-EXP-002_THE_HIDDEN_CAVE_V001.jpg": "Dark cave interior with a shaft of light from a high opening at centre-right and no people. A rock arch at left frames an entrance with ivy hanging over rubble. The floor is covered in rocks and leaf litter, with a small trickle of water at lower left. The walls show layered rock faces.",
"ENV_CH05-INT-001_THE_HERDERS_SHELTER_V001.jpg": "Open-fronted shelter built against a cliff of stacked stone, with no people. A grass thatch roof rests on timber poles, with a woven wattle panel at right. Inside is a low stone bench with folded blankets or hides, and a clay pot sits outside. A rope loop hangs from the frame and a walking stick leans on the wall. A dry golden hillside and mountains lie beyond under blue sky.",
"ENV_CH05-INT-002_A_VILLAGE_HOUSE_V001.jpg": "Stone-and-mud cottage with a steep thatched roof under heavy rain, and no people. Through the doorway a hearth with flames and a cooking pot is visible, with a shelf of pots and jars, a low bed with fur covering in a recess, a stool, a basket and a bowl of grain. A heavy plank door with an iron latch sits at right. Other thatched cottages and dark mountains stand in the background.",
"ENV_CH05-LMK-002_THE_ABANDONED_WATCHPOST_V001.jpg": "Small round stone tower on a grassy hilltop, with its roof gone and splayed poles at the top, and no people. A timber-framed doorway opens to a dark interior, with a rubble heap beside it at right. Layered mountains with snow-streaked peaks lie beyond under overcast sky.",
"ENV_CH05-SET-002_THE_UPPER_HAMLET_V001.jpg": "Hillside village of stone cottages with thatched roofs, some with chimneys, and no people. Stone terrace walls and stepped paths link the houses around an open grassy space. Mountains and cloud fill the background under overcast light.",
"ENV_CH05-SUB-003_THE_CLIMBERS_CAMP_V001.jpg": "Painted view on a sheer rock face above cloud-filled valleys, with peaks in the distance and no people. On a ledge in the foreground are two A-frame lean-to shelters, one with a grass or thatch top and one with a stretched hide or cloth panel. A wooden ladder leans against the rock, with a stone fire ring, coiled rope and a bundle of poles nearby.",
"ENV_CH06-INT-004_A_ROOM_THAT_EXPECTS_YOU_V001.jpg": "Plain room with pale grey-green walls and a reflective grey floor, with no people. A single white bed with a white pillow and sheet sits at right, next to a bedside table holding a white mug. A wooden chair with a grey upholstered back faces away from the viewer. A chest with a potted green plant, a framed picture and a wall sconce are at left. An open door leads to a dark corridor, and a window on the right shows a night sky.",
"ENV_CH06-INT-005_THE_FORGOTTEN_ROOM_V001.jpg": "Decayed room with stained, peeling plaster walls, a dusty wooden floor and dry leaves, with no people. A tall carved wardrobe stands with one door hanging open. A clouded old framed mirror hangs on the wall. A large object at right is covered by a sheet of gauze-like fabric, with a fireplace and dried flowers at the far right edge. Tattered sheer curtains hang at a window at left, and cobwebs fill the corners.",
"B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_BACK_V003_2560x1440.png": "Four-view sheet titled ADANNA, TURNAROUND: BACK, plate 3 of 4, on a dark UI frame. The main panel is a full back view on light grey: braids in a high knot, indigo bandeau, indigo wrap skirt, diagonal leather strap and a bronze armlet on the viewer-left arm, leather sandals. The sidebar lists asset, label, source, seven corrections, locks checked and open qualifications. Labels read EXPLORATORY, NOT APPROVED CANON, STATUS REVIEW REQUIRED, UNAPPROVED, PENDING REVIEW. The sidebar says it supersedes V002 and that no blade is depicted.",
"B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_FRONT_V003_2560x1440.png": "Four-view sheet titled ADANNA, TURNAROUND: FRONT, plate 1 of 4, V003. The main panel shows a full front view on light grey: braided knot, indigo bandeau and wrap, a leather baldric from the viewer-right shoulder to the viewer-left hip, bronze armlet, leather sandals. Sidebar and footer carry the labels EXPLORATORY, NOT APPROVED CANON, STATUS REVIEW REQUIRED, UNAPPROVED, PENDING REVIEW, with an open-items list for the blade, scabbard and armlet.",
"B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_FRONT_V004_2560x1440.png": "Four-view sheet titled ADANNA, TURNAROUND: FRONT, plate 1 of 4, V004. The front figure wears indigo bandeau and wrap, a leather baldric, a bronze armlet on the viewer-left arm and sandals, and no blade. The sidebar lists corrections 1 to 7 from V003 and corrections 8 and 9 for V004, including the pendant cord now running to the neck. Footer: EXPLORATORY, NOT APPROVED CANON, UNAPPROVED, PENDING REVIEW.",
"B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_LEFT_SIDE_V003_2560x1440.png": "Four-view sheet titled ADANNA, TURNAROUND: LEFT SIDE, plate 2 of 4, V003. A full left-profile figure on light grey: braided high knot with beaded braid tips, indigo bandeau, indigo wrap skirt, a leather strap over the shoulder, a bronze armlet on the upper arm and leather sandals. Sidebar lists the seven V003 corrections and open items. Footer: EXPLORATORY, NOT APPROVED CANON, UNAPPROVED, PENDING REVIEW.",
"B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_THREE_QUARTER_V003_2560x1440.png": "Four-view sheet titled ADANNA, TURNAROUND: THREE QUARTER, plate 4 of 4, V003. A three-quarter standing figure on light grey: braided knot, indigo bandeau, indigo wrap with a knot at the side, a leather baldric from the viewer-left shoulder to the viewer-right hip, a pendant at the neck, bronze armlet and leather sandals. Sidebar lists V003 corrections. Footer: EXPLORATORY, NOT APPROVED CANON, UNAPPROVED, PENDING REVIEW.",
"B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_THREE_QUARTER_V004_2560x1440.png": "Four-view sheet titled ADANNA, TURNAROUND: THREE QUARTER, plate 4 of 4, V004. The figure matches V003, with the pendant cord visibly at the neck. Sidebar lists V003 corrections 1 to 7 and V004 corrections 8 and 9. Footer: EXPLORATORY, NOT APPROVED CANON, UNAPPROVED, PENDING REVIEW.",
"B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-006_A_LARGE_FAMILY_COMPOUND_V002_1672x941.jpg": "Photographic-style courtyard under overcast sky, with red earth and no people. Indigo cloths and clay pots with gourds hang on a mud wall at left. An open plank double gate in the centre leads to a dark interior and a thatched hut. At right is a thatched open-sided shelter on timber posts, with firewood, a mortar and pestle, a low bench and clay pots. Grain is spread on a woven mat with a sieve at lower right. Footer: SCENE CH01-SCN-006, a large family compound, V002, exploratory, not approved canon, status review required.",
"B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-010_SMITHY_V002_1672x941.jpg": "Open-sided mud-walled smithy at sunset, with village huts behind and no people. A clay hearth holds glowing charcoal, with two leather bellows beside it. Iron tongs, a hammer, an anvil block and dark iron blanks lie on the floor. Tools hang on the back wall, with a log trough and clay pots at right. Footer: SCENE CH01-SCN-010, smithy, V002, exploratory, not approved canon, status review required.",
"B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-012_MARKET_STALLS_V002_1672x941.jpg": "Village market at golden hour, with palms and mud-brick compounds behind and no people. Thatched and mat-roofed stalls on timber poles hold piled produce: green chillies or peppers, red fruit in bowls, yams or cassava, green bananas and gourds. Cloth lies folded on a low table at left, and woven mats lean against a wall. Footer: SCENE CH01-SCN-012, market stalls, V002, exploratory, status review required.",
"B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-017_VILLAGE_SQUARE_V002_1672x941.jpg": "Dusty village lane at sunset, with no people. Mud-walled compounds with pointed parapets and conical thatch roofs line the lane. A large shade tree at right shelters a wooden bench, with a stone mortar and pestle and clay pots at the right edge. Rows of thatched huts fade into haze in the background. Footer: SCENE CH01-SCN-017, village square, V002, exploratory, status review required.",
"B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-022_STREETS_V002_1672x941.jpg": "Narrow earthen lane between mud walls at sunset, with no people. A timber lattice canopy with thatch crosses the lane overhead. Gourds hang from a pole at right, with a cream cloth on a line and a clay pot and a mortar and pestle at ground level. A plank doorway is set into the wall at left. Footer: SCENE CH01-SCN-022, streets, V002, exploratory, status review required.",
"B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-032_WELLS_V002_1672x941.jpg": "Village yard with two round mud-rimmed wells, a rope and a gourd bowl, and no people. A goat stands at left beside thatched huts. A woodpile, a shallow drainage channel and a broken clay pot lie in the foreground. Footer: SCENE CH01-SCN-032, wells, V002, exploratory, status review required.",
"B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-033_GATES_V002_1672x941.jpg": "Timber post-and-lintel gateway over a dirt path, with brushwood fence panels on mud walls on either side and no people. Beyond the gate are thatched huts, palms and rolling hills. Footer: SCENE CH01-SCN-033, gates, V002, exploratory, status review required.",
"B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-034_ROADS_V002_1672x941.jpg": "Dirt lane between red mud-brick walls, with thatched roofs above and no people. Two doorways at right carry blue cloth hangings. A puddle, scattered sherds and a fallen branch lie on the ground. Palms and trees show in the background. Footer: SCENE CH01-SCN-034, roads, V002, exploratory, status review required.",
"B2_CAND_VR-011_LANDING_OF_UNCLAIMED_V002_2560x1440.png": "Design sheet titled THE GATES OF THE DEAD, THE LANDING OF THE UNCLAIMED, labelled ENV_GATES_DEAD_LANDING_OF_UNCLAIMED_V001, status review required, environment chapter 7 batch 4. The sidebar gives register CH07-SUB-004, scene CH07-SCN-011, PROPOSED, with use, read, story, gameplay and known-issues text. The image shows grey dugout canoes drawn up on a mudflat, with bundles, pots and folded cloth inside, and a long mud rampart at right with poles carrying pale cloth strips. Still water lies at left under overcast sky. Footer: entirely fictional, design PROPOSED, not canon.",
"B2_COMPARE_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_V002_alignment.jpg": "Four-panel orthographic sheet titled ADANNA, TURNAROUND V002, labelled candidate for review, not an approved asset, with no blade depicted and CQ-9 OPEN. Panels are FRONT, LEFT SIDE, BACK and THREE QUARTER, each a full figure on grey with matching floor and crown lines. Text lines give height spread 4 px, crown spread 0 px, floor spread 4 px. The text states the baldric runs over the RIGHT shoulder to the LEFT hip, and that the armlet, temple beads and cheek scar sit on the anatomical LEFT.",
"B2_COMPARE_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_V003_alignment.jpg": "Four-panel orthographic sheet titled ADANNA, TURNAROUND V003, labelled exploratory, not approved canon, status review required, unapproved, pending review. Panels are 1 FRONT, 2 LEFT SIDE, 3 BACK and 4 THREE QUARTER, each a full figure on grey. Metrics: height spread 4 px, crown spread 0 px, floor spread 4 px. The text states the baldric runs over the anatomical LEFT shoulder to the anatomical RIGHT hip, and that the armlet and beads stay on the anatomical LEFT. It notes that V001 and V002 are preserved in a rejected-designs folder.",
"B2_COMPARE_COSTUME_BREAKDOWN_V001_vs_V002.jpg": "Comparison sheet headed ADANNA, COSTUME BREAKDOWN, V001 rejected to V002 candidate. The left panel is V001, marked unapproved, pending CD, with front callouts, a back panel stamped UNRESOLVED, NOT APPROVED, a right-side panel marked plain by design, and crops of the temple beads and armlet. The right panel is V002 candidate, marked unapproved, with hatched placeholders labelled RIGHT SIDE PLAIN BY DESIGN, BACK TORSO UNRESOLVED and LOWER BODY and WEAPON UNRESOLVED, an identity-lock list, a tag key and a palette strip. Some footer lines run off the right edge.",
"B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING.jpg": "Side-by-side ESTABLISHING VIEW for ENV_LAST_DAUGHTER_ANCESTRAL_REALM_ESTABLISHING, V005 review-required on the left and V006 candidate on the right. Both show a long colonnaded hall at left, a tiered settlement mound at right under a pale river band, and thatched mud houses in the foreground. The candidate mound is an irregular stack of separate houses, and no figure appears in the yard. Text lines below describe the defect, the resolution and a note that no V006 exists in the drive.",
"B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V005_vs_V007.jpg": "Comparison sheet headed ESTABLISHING VIEW, ANCESTRAL REALM, V005 base to V007 candidate, a masked architectural repaint of the settlement mound. The base shows a symmetrical tiered mound at right. The candidate shows an irregular heap of single-storey houses with ladders and stair runs, with soft haze at the mask edge. Insets show the mound and the mound foot before and after. Text lines list defects A to C, pixel proof, open items and status.",
"B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V005_vs_V008.jpg": "Comparison sheet headed ESTABLISHING VIEW, ANCESTRAL REALM, V005 base to V008 candidate, a masked mound rebuild at village scale with the chrome repaired. The base shows a tiered mound; the candidate shows a dense accumulation of many small houses forming the mound, with a new aerial river along its flank. Insets show the mound and the aerial river before and after. Text lines list defects, pixel proof, requirement D as not delivered and status.",
"B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V008_vs_V009.jpg": "Sheet headed ESTABLISHING, V008 to V009 candidate. It describes option A for requirement D, with the foreground compound re-staged, Nneka's House and a staked plot placed in warm daylight. Top cards show V008 superseded and V009 candidate. Insets show A the mound foot with a hard seam becoming drifting dust, B a lower-right mist veil warm-corrected, C the right compound changed from a cramped longhouse to an open yard with a thatched house, staked plot and clothes line, and D Nneka's House and plot at 1:1 and 2x.",
"B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V009_vs_V010.jpg": "Sheet headed ESTABLISHING, V009 to V010 candidate. It describes one correction: the hill dwellings re-scaled to the plain, with the foreground compound, Hall of Posts and left compound untouched. Top cards show V009 superseded and V010 candidate. Insets show A the hill with dwellings about 30 percent smaller and roughly twice as many, B the hill foot, C the right compound unchanged, and D the hill at 2x.",
"B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V010_vs_V011_CHROME.jpg": "Text-only comparison of register and client-review blocks on dark background. The V010 block reads CLIENT REVIEW, REVISE, tenth, hill dwellings re-scaled to the plain, right-hand compound unchanged, presented as a stale round label. The V011 block reads CLIENT REVIEW, PENDING, with no client ruling recorded and candidate only. Footers read exploratory, not approved canon, consultant review required, figureless by client decision. Bottom line reads panel pixels 0 changed, chrome 8,046 px.",
"B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V011_vs_V012.jpg": "Sheet headed ESTABLISHING, V011 to V012 candidate, four zones corrected and chrome rebuilt, with item 1 house scale not attempted and stated as such. Top cards show V011 superseded and V012 candidate. Insets show A the yard with the paling gone and the cloth line whole, B the wall behind the paling with an in-context patch, C the lower-right wall with its blue cast corrected to warm earth, and D the cloth line at 2x with striped cloths restored. Text lines describe items 2 and 3.",
"B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V012_vs_V013.jpg": "Diagnostic comparison headed ESTABLISHING VIEW, V012 vs V013, candidate unapproved. Panel A compares the frame margin and lower-right wall, with RGB values noted. Panel B compares the cloth line at the right end: V012 has a hard seam and pale wedge, V013 has the edge re-rendered as fabric. Panel C compares Nneka's House: V012 reads large with no striped side cloth, and V013 is about 15 percent smaller with the approved side cloth restored. Measurement lines list house height 227 px in V012 and 193 px in V013.",
"B2_COMPARE_VR-008.jpg": "Comparison headed VR-008, COMP_ADANNA_SEALED_QUARTER_HAND_ON_SEAL, V005 review-required to V006 candidate. Left and right panels show a woman in an indigo top with a bronze pauldron, her hand flat on a plastered seal panel in a narrow earthen lane, with a bowl and pot at left and thatch at top. The candidate panel shows a more prominent, branched crack on the seal. Text lines state the defect, the hand-retouch method, zero change outside the panel and candidate status.",
"B2_COMPARE_VR-008_V005_to_V008_with_references.jpg": "Comparison headed VR-008, V005 base to V008 candidate, hand retouch only. Two full panels show the same woman with her hand on the seal, bronze pauldron, indigo top, belt, a sheathed weapon at the left hip, bowl and pot. Reference strips show defect B the midriff, defect C the armlet with the master portrait, V007 and V008 side by side, and defect A the fracture in V005 and V008. Text lines list defects A to D, pixel proof, untouched elements and status.",
"B2_COMPARE_VR-008_V005_vs_V007.jpg": "Before and after panels headed VR-008, V005 review-required to V007 candidate, with no generative pass and zero changed pixels outside the masks. The composition is the same in both. Changes visible: the seal crack is now a warm dark-umber fracture, and the armlet is a painted dull band rather than multi-coil bronze. Insets show the midriff, the left upper arm armlet and the fracture before and after. Text lines list defects A to D and pixel proof.",
"B2_COMPARE_VR-008_V008_vs_V009.jpg": "Composition sheet headed VR-008 SEALED QUARTER, V008 to V009 candidate. The V008 card is rejected and the V009 card is the candidate. Insets show A the left shoulder, with the bronze pauldron in V008 and a bare brown shoulder with a thin leather strap in V009, B the coiled bronze armlet preserved in both, and C the sheet chrome. Text lines state the pauldron was removed, gains preserved, and the candidate is unapproved.",
"B2_COMPARE_VR-010.jpg": "Comparison headed VR-010, ENV_HOME_SETTLEMENT_WASHING_PLACE, V002 review-required to V003 candidate. Left V002 and right V003 show a walled washing place with a palm-frond screen, a large flat wet stone slab, pots, a leaf, chewing sticks and a sponge. The V003 candidate has a stone-lined culvert mouth set into the base of the compound wall at lower left, and the bright wet channel is absent from the open ground. Text lines give the defect, the resolution, secondary drift and zero change outside the panel.",
"B2_COMPARE_VR-010_WASHING_PLACE_V002_vs_V004.jpg": "Comparison headed WASHING PLACE, ANCESTRAL REALM, V002 base to V004 candidate, masked removal of the exposed runoff channel. The base shows a wet bright channel across the ground beside the slab. The candidate has no channel; the ground reads as plain damp earth. Pots, dipper, slab, leaf, sticks and straw are the same in both. Insets show the channel and the slab area before and after. Text lines list defects 1 to 7, pixel proof, declared deviation and status.",
"B2_COMPARE_VR-010_WASHING_PLACE_V002_vs_V005.jpg": "Comparison headed WASHING PLACE, HOME SETTLEMENT, V002 base to V005 candidate, chrome only. The base card is labelled runoff channel present. The candidate card shows a flush grade with no channel and the outlet off-frame. Insets show the channel, the flush ground, the slab with pots and soap, and the woven screen with no wall opening. Text lines list defects 1 to 5, unchanged elements and status.",
"B2_COMPARE_VR-011.jpg": "Comparison headed VR-011, ENV_GATES_DEAD_LANDING_OF_UNCLAIMED, V001 review-required to V002 candidate. Left and right views show grey dugout canoes drawn up on a mudflat under overcast sky, with bundles and pots in the foreground canoe, a long mud rampart with poles and pale cloth strips at right, and still water at left. The candidate strips hang straight and the canoe field is denser. Text lines give the defects addressed, resolution, residual and chapter 7 status.",
"B2_COMPARE_WALL_OF_HOUSES.jpg": "Comparison headed WALL OF HOUSES, ENV_LAST_DAUGHTER_ANCESTRAL_REALM_WALL_OF_HOUSES, V003 review-required to V004 candidate. Both show a hillside of mud-brick houses in fog with thatch roofs. The candidate shows the houses at the foot as freestanding dwellings with gaps between them, and the sealed doorways as pale plastered panels, one with a visible crack. Text lines give the defects addressed, resolution and residual.",
"B2_COMPARE_WALL_OF_HOUSES_V003_vs_V005.jpg": "Comparison headed WALL OF HOUSES, ANCESTRAL REALM, V003 base to V005 candidate, a masked repaint of the built mound. The base shows a fogged mound of stacked two-storey blocks. The candidate shows single-storey houses and a separate older first settlement at the foot, with two small thatched huts, one with a plain sealed doorway. Insets show the first settlement and three doorway states: lit, dark and plain-sealed. Text lines list defects A to F, pixel proof, open items and status.",
"B2_PIXELDIFF_VR-008_V007.jpg": "Dark pixel-difference map of the VR-008 panel from V005 to V007, showing a woman in profile at a plastered door with her hand raised, with a bowl and pot at lower left. Three green labelled boxes mark A fracture 1,504 px, B midriff 8,481 px and C armlet 3,633 px, with white changed-pixel masks inside them. Caption text: 13,618 of 2,222,269 pixels changed (0.61 percent), all inside the three declared masks.",
"B2_RETOUCH_GUIDE_VR-006_BLOCKED.jpg": "Opened and viewed; not blocked. Composition titled ADANNA IN THE MOTHERS' COURTYARD, COMP_ADANNA_MOTHERS_COURTYARD_V003, status review required. A thatched shelter holds a loom with striped cloth, jars, a mortar and pestle, and a tree with a broom. A woman in an indigo top with a bronze shoulder piece stands in an open doorway, her hand on the mortar. Overlay titled VR-006 RETOUCH GUIDE, one object only, marks A hilt at the left hip (keep) and B the current sheath tip, with a target to hang the sheath vertically. Side text includes location CH08-SUB-005, assessment requires revision, and scabbard check. Palette strip of seven browns.",
"B2_RETOUCH_GUIDE_VR-007_BLOCKED.jpg": "Opened and viewed; not blocked. Composition titled ADANNA INSIDE NNEKA'S HOUSE, COMP_ADANNA_NNEKAS_HOUSE_INTERIOR_V002, status review required. A mud house interior with a pole-and-thatch roof and an open doorway shows a striped cloth outside. A seated figure in a blue wrap and indigo top with a metal shoulder piece sits on a sleeping platform, with a long sheath along it. Hearth stones and a pot, a basket of cotton, jars and a woven mat are present. Overlay titled VR-007 RETOUCH GUIDE, one object only, marks A spiral pommel (keep) and B chape disc (move up), with a target tip no lower than a marked line. Side text covers location CH08-INT-001, assessment, recurring fault and story note.",
"CAND_ESTABLISHING_V013_2560x1440.png": "Establishing view titled ANCESTRAL REALM, ENV_LAST_DAUGHTER_ANCESTRAL_REALM_ESTABLISHING_V013, status review required, exploratory, not approved canon, chapter 8. A long colonnaded hall at left, a tiered mound of stacked houses with ladders at right under a pale river band, thatched mud houses in the foreground, and a small thatched house with a yard of stakes and a line of cloth at lower centre. Sidebar lists changes since V012: lower-right wall rewarmed, frame margin bleed removed, cloth line repaired, Nneka's House about 15 percent smaller. Also lists not-fixed items and fictional elements. Footer: exploratory, not approved canon, unapproved.",
"ENV_CH03-INT-004_THE_FORGOTTEN_KITCHEN_V002.jpg": "Monochrome dusty interior with no people. A dark round-bellied cooking pot sits on three stones over a pile of ash. Bundles of dried herbs hang from a pole on the back wall, and a dark doorway opens at right. A stone quern and a shallow bowl sit at far right. An open doorway at left shows bare trees and snow-dusted ground.",
"ENV_CH03-INT-005_A_SLEEPING_ROOM_V002.jpg": "Monochrome dim interior seen through a wooden-framed doorway, with no people. A raised wooden platform holds a woven mat and two folded cloths. Cobwebs hang in the ceiling corners. A large clay jar and a small bowl sit on the earthen floor at right.",
"ENV_CH03-SUB-005_A_RESIDENTIAL_COURTYARD_V002.jpg": "Monochrome courtyard in falling speckle, with no people. Two indigo cloths hang on a rope above a low mud-plastered wall at left. At right, a thatched hut has a wooden mortar and pestle and two rolled woven mats leaning against it. A small carved wooden bird sits on the ground in front.",
"ENV_CH03-SUB-006_THE_BACK_PLOTS_V002.jpg": "Monochrome back plot under grey sky, with no people. A thatched mud house stands at left and a wattle fence at right. Dry maize stalks grow at left. A hoe stands upright in the grey mud at centre, and a cracked clay jar lies on its side at right. Other thatched houses and bare trees stand in the background.",
"ENV_CH03-TRV-003_THE_NARROW_PASSAGES_V002.jpg": "Monochrome narrow passage between two tall plastered walls, with no people. Footprints lead away along the grey ground. A narrow strip of sky shows at the top, and small particles drift in the air.",
"ENV_CH04-INT-001_A_FISHING_SHELTER_V002.jpg": "Open-sided shelter with a thatched roof on timber posts, with no people. Fishing nets hang from the roof beams. Wicker traps and baskets are at left, and a wooden board with a knife lies in the foreground. A long wooden rack stands at right, with the river beyond.",
"ENV_CH04-INT-002_A_RIVERBANK_HOUSE_V002.jpg": "Mud-walled house with a thatched roof on the riverbank, with no people. Its open door shows a platform with a rack of fish at the front. Clay pots, baskets and a folded cloth sit on the ground. A dugout canoe lies at the water's edge at right, with palms and river behind.",
"ENV_CH04-INT-003_THE_CANOE_SHED_V002.jpg": "Open shed with a thatched roof on timber posts, with no people. Three dugout canoes rest on log cradles; the front one is being carved, with an adze lying across it. Wood chips cover the ground. An axe with a wooden handle leans against a post at right, with the river and trees visible beyond.",
"ENV_CH04-SET-002_THE_TWO_HOUSE_LANDING_V002.jpg": "Two thatched mud houses stand either side of a red-earth path that leads into palm forest, with no people. A wooden rack at right holds a row of fish. Two dugout canoes float in the water in the foreground, below a bank of red earth.",
}
